{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/933374-what-to-take-out-of-the-system-if-not-using-it-for-supernatural-horror","id":933374,"title":"What to take out of the system if not using it for supernatural/horror?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-18T05:33:57-07:00","id":933374,"title":"What to take out of the system if not using it for supernatural/horror?","content":"<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Hello! I posed this question on Reddit, but was hoping for more response. So, my apologies to anyone who I'm subjecting this to more that once!<br /> <br /> I new to running a Chronicles of Darkness game (though I've read over the rules) and was going to use the system to run a modern dramatic/gritty game (of crime and corruption) where the players will range from normal folk to about one step below street-level supers. In my perusal of the rules I got to wondering what - in the community's opinion - I should leave out. The only thing I can see that sticks out in a non-horror, non-supernatural is the Occult skill. My Reddit replies convinced me that Occult does have a place in a non-supernatural/non-horror game, though. Anyway, I was hoping to get some feedback about any rules changes you all would make. Thanks!</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12124-lord-dynel","name":"Lord Dynel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12124_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-18T06:03:39-07:00","id":933381,"title":"","content":"Integrity. If you're not running a horror game then integrity needs to either be reworked or removed entirely. Occult can remain like reddit said, just removes the whole &quot;these things you know from occult research might actually be true&quot; aspect that CoD usually has. A few merits would obviously be disallowed (like all supernatural merits and mystery cult initiation).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-18T06:14:25-07:00","id":933384,"title":"","content":"Actually, I'd leave in Integrity. Integrity isn't what makes vanilla CofD a horror game. Like, if you renamed Integrity to Stress and flipped it so that high Stress = bad and low Stress = good, you're golden, right? So just leave Integrity as-is. You could even add some Conditions like &quot;Tempted&quot; that you could give to players after Integrity Breaking Points if they're gonna be working in an environment that breeds corruption.<br /> <br /> Mystery Cult Initiation still works, because the Freemasons exist. Mystery Cult Initiation doesn't have to have a literal magical artifact at the center.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-18T06:31:37-07:00","id":933392,"title":"","content":"Nothing except for supernatural merits. CofD is very well suited for politically focused games, and as you have noted, even the occult skill is still totally valid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-18T07:53:59-07:00","id":933415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/933374-what-to-take-out-of-the-system-if-not-using-it-for-supernatural-horror?p=933392#post933392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nothing except for supernatural merits. CofD is very well suited for politically focused games, and as you have noted, even the occult skill is still totally valid.</div> </div> </div> </div>I used CofD for a dystopian future game set within a North America-wide rebellion against a dictatorship. I honestly did have to make any changes at all (beyond telling my players they were all mundane).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-18T07:58:10-07:00","id":933419,"title":"","content":"OP, a lot of the content here is background info for the game itself, but if it would help, there are also some posts about new statuses I made (Like Status (Rebellion) ) that might help you form similar things. No worries if it's not helpful, just wanted to include it in case it would help =).<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://torren-s-north-america.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://torren-s-north-america.obsidianportal.com/</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-18T07:59:07-07:00","id":933421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fumus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/933374-what-to-take-out-of-the-system-if-not-using-it-for-supernatural-horror?p=933381#post933381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Integrity. If you're not running a horror game then integrity needs to either be reworked or removed entirely. Occult can remain like reddit said, just removes the whole &quot;these things you know from occult research might actually be true&quot; aspect that CoD usually has. A few merits would obviously be disallowed (like all supernatural merits and mystery cult initiation).</div> </div> </div> </div>Heck, given the comment about &quot;<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">one step below street-level supers</span></span></span>&quot;, not even all of the Supernatural merits need to be thrown out. The Lost Boys in the Hurt Locker preview aren't very &quot;supernatural&quot;, and things like Omen Sensitivity can represent instinctive or honed pattern recognition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-18T10:02:54-07:00","id":933464,"title":"","content":"There's really nothing mechanical about CofD that is intrinsically tied to supernatural horror. I have seen a lot of crossover between players who don't like the personal horror themes and players who don't like Integrity and it's analogue traits, but as other folks here have pointed out, it could easily have a place in non-horror games as well. Things like theme and mood really have more to do with how you run your game and how you narrate things than the mechanics. Pretty much, keep what ever mechanical elements you like and throw out the ones you don't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-18T13:14:14-07:00","id":933549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/933374-what-to-take-out-of-the-system-if-not-using-it-for-supernatural-horror?p=933419#post933419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OP, a lot of the content here is background info for the game itself, but if it would help, there are also some posts about new statuses I made (Like Status (Rebellion) ) that might help you form similar things. No worries if it's not helpful, just wanted to include it in case it would help =).<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://torren-s-north-america.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://torren-s-north-america.obsidianportal.com/</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for the link. I will definitely check it out!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12124-lord-dynel","name":"Lord Dynel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12124_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-18T13:23:43-07:00","id":933555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/933374-what-to-take-out-of-the-system-if-not-using-it-for-supernatural-horror?p=933464#post933464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's really nothing mechanical about CofD that is intrinsically tied to supernatural horror. I have seen a lot of crossover between players who don't like the personal horror themes and players who don't like Integrity and it's analogue traits, but as other folks here have pointed out, it could easily have a place in non-horror games as well. Things like theme and mood really have more to do with how you run your game and how you narrate things than the mechanics. Pretty much, keep what ever mechanical elements you like and throw out the ones you don't.</div> </div> </div> </div>True enough. There are things that lend themselves more to a supernatural game than not, though, it seems. Things like the Dread Powers and the Numina, though some I can reskin to low level powers (Like Immortal ninjas, ala <i>Daredevil</i>), if I want to go that route. Most characters will be human-scale in power, though. I might include a roided-up brute-type to be an enforcer for a mob boss (think Crossbones from Marvel comics, nothing too super about him, he's just damn strong and can fight) but that's probably the extent of it. <br /> <br /> Maybe a better question would be, what sourcebooks would best fit the type of game I want to run? I've got Antagonists, Armory, Tales of the 13th Precinct, Armory Reloaded (on order), Mirrors (also on order), Slasher, and I'm contemplating the Hunter core book. I know the intention of WW/OP was to have games liberally laced with the supernatural, but I'm curious what books might be better suited to (or at least have good portions usable for) a primarily mortal game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12124-lord-dynel","name":"Lord Dynel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12124_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T07:14:02-07:00","id":933856,"title":"","content":"<i><a href=\"http://drivethrurpg.com/product/56496/World-of-Darkness-Dogs-of-War\" target=\"_blank\">World of Darkness: Dogs of War</a></i> is all about military characters in the way that <i>Tales of the 13th Precinct </i>is about police officers.<br /> <a href=\"http://drivethrurpg.com/product/28796/Damnation-City\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Damnation City</i></a> is technically a Vampire book but it's fantastic for <i>all</i> CofD games as far as I'm concerned.<br /> <i><a href=\"http://drivethrurpg.com/product/55727/World-of-Darkness-Innocents\" target=\"_blank\">Innocents</a> </i>could work if you want to involve children.<br /> <br /> Nothing else is coming to mind, but I've never tried to run a non-supernatural game. Hopefully some other people can make some good suggestions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T07:42:04-07:00","id":933873,"title":"","content":"Although it's certainly a judgment call, I would also endorse dropping integrity. With some notable exceptions, the fear of losing one's mind is much less a trope of urban grit than of horror. Depending on the particular story you're planning to tell, using Breaking Point mechanics could be out-of-genre and alienating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12108-gscrap","name":"gscrap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12108_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T09:06:44-07:00","id":933928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gscrap</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/933374-what-to-take-out-of-the-system-if-not-using-it-for-supernatural-horror?p=933873#post933873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although it's certainly a judgment call, I would also endorse dropping integrity. With some notable exceptions, the fear of losing one's mind is much less a trope of urban grit than of horror. Depending on the particular story you're planning to tell, using Breaking Point mechanics could be out-of-genre and alienating.</div> </div> </div> </div>Integrity loss doesn't really cause one to &quot;lose their mind&quot;, though. It causes post-traumatic stress symptoms (and I guess the Madness Condition, but you could just not use that one, since it doesn't represent any actual psychological condition that exists).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T01:22:59-07:00","id":934348,"title":"","content":"I'm gonna throw in my 2 cents on this:<br /> <br /> There is nothing that one needs to change about WoD to make it a non-horror game. The only thing that makes it &quot;horror&quot; is the way the Storyteller weaves the narrative. If you go look at other books in the engine, such as Scion, you'll see that it's perfectly possible to use the underlying engine for things like a fantastical jaunt through a pile of not-so-scary monsters which your character is bashing around with a giant hammer, or to play a campaign that literally revolves around a group of politicians trying to prevent a declaration of war. Hell, even with supernatural elements, things aren't horror: go look at stuff like Blade, My Little Pony, and Harry Potter. For all their supernatural elements, they don't really scare you, because 1) the villain is both knowable and defeatable, and 2) while potentially intense and/or scary, they don't play up the factors which give you that bone chilling fear that makes a REAL horror story.<br /> <br /> Yeah, sure, Buffy is fighting Vampires and shit, but we barely ever see the monsters doing anything that invokes a deeper fear than hunting humans, and Buffy just kicks their ass by the end of the episode anyway.<br /> <br /> One of the last campaigns I was in was a medieval adventure involving military strategy, intrigue, and monster hunting. The only change the ST made to the core rules was to not involve the supernatural elements. It went really well in the system, though the one problem was that <b>The Storyteller Engine is made for plot-heavy mechanic-loose play, and does not lend itself to action-movie combat</b>. Even with that, we had two combat heavy characters in the party and a few different military battles, and everything went fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T03:03:08-07:00","id":934372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RockstarRaccoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/933374-what-to-take-out-of-the-system-if-not-using-it-for-supernatural-horror?p=934348#post934348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is nothing that one needs to change about WoD to make it a non-horror game. The only thing that makes it &quot;horror&quot; is the way the Storyteller weaves the narrative. If you go look at other books in the engine, such as Scion, you'll see that it's perfectly possible to use the underlying engine for things like a fantastical jaunt through a pile of not-so-scary monsters which your character is bashing around with a giant hammer, or to play a campaign that literally revolves around a group of politicians trying to prevent a declaration of war. </div> </div> </div> </div>Storypath isn't the same as the storytelling system, mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T09:13:12-07:00","id":934525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RockstarRaccoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/933374-what-to-take-out-of-the-system-if-not-using-it-for-supernatural-horror?p=934348#post934348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hell, even with supernatural elements, things aren't horror: go look at stuff like Blade, My Little Pony, and Harry Potter. For all their supernatural elements, they don't really scare you, because 1) the villain is both knowable and defeatable, and 2) while potentially intense and/or scary, they don't play up the factors which give you that bone chilling fear that makes a REAL horror story.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've often said that the difference between an action story and a horror story is whether the protagonists understand what they're up against, allowing them to effectively strategize. The difference between Alien and Aliens, or the difference between Poltergeist and Ghostbusters.<br /> <br /> With that in mind, it can be really hard to make a horror story in any of the nWoD splats except for maybe human-only Core and Innocents, because the protagonists in a Werewolf or Vampire story tend to understand very well what they're up against. It becomes less a game of gothic horror, and more a gothic character drama. Which I'm cool with, honestly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12108-gscrap","name":"gscrap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12108_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T09:19:00-07:00","id":934533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gscrap</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/933374-what-to-take-out-of-the-system-if-not-using-it-for-supernatural-horror?p=934525#post934525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've often said that the difference between an action story and a horror story is whether the protagonists understand what they're up against, allowing them to effectively strategize. The difference between Alien and Aliens, or the difference between Poltergeist and Ghostbusters.<br /> <br /> With that in mind, it can be really hard to make a horror story in any of the nWoD splats except for maybe human-only Core and Innocents, because<b> the protagonists in a Werewolf or Vampire story tend to understand very well what they're up against</b>. It becomes less a game of gothic horror, and more a gothic character drama. Which I'm cool with, honestly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Funny. Strix. Idigam.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T10:34:42-07:00","id":934578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gscrap</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/933374-what-to-take-out-of-the-system-if-not-using-it-for-supernatural-horror?p=934525#post934525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've often said that the difference between an action story and a horror story is whether the protagonists understand what they're up against, allowing them to effectively strategize. The difference between Alien and Aliens, or the difference between Poltergeist and Ghostbusters.<br /> <br /> With that in mind, it can be really hard to make a horror story in any of the nWoD splats except for maybe human-only Core and Innocents, because the protagonists in a Werewolf or Vampire story tend to understand very well what they're up against. It becomes less a game of gothic horror, and more a gothic character drama. Which I'm cool with, honestly.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a fine definition for external horror, but CofD has always been more focused on personal horror. To quote John Carpenter,<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u201cThere are two horror stories that we can tell, and we can imagine ourselves around the campfire listening to the tribal elder or witch doctor or preacher or whoever it is telling us these things at night. The first thing he tells us is about where \u2018evil\u2019 is, and he says, \u2018Evil is out there,\u2019 and he points beyond the campfire, to the darkness in the woods and the noises we hear at night; the wolves that come and drag us off; those beasts out there; the \u2018other\u2019 - the other tribe, the other people - the ones who are different, different color, their eyes are different from ours; those are the evil ones out there. In different countries they have different clothes, different ideologies, or they may be any force of nature we cannot control, so this unifies the tribe.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s the first story of horror. The second one is the same setup, but the tribal elder says, \u2018Let me tell you where the evil is - the evil is here,\u2019 and he points to himself. And he says, \u2018It\u2019s in the human heart.\u2019 That\u2019s a harder story to tell - that we are all part evil, monsters and devils - because the audience is always going to respond to the \u2018other.\u2019 It unifies us as a tribe - that\u2019s the way we are designed. We see things in order to find where the predator comes from; it\u2019s survival instinct over all the time we have evolved. So a lot of this is unconscious in a way. We\u2019re driven by it, and our parents reinforce it, our religion reinforces it \u2013 \u2018Watch out!\u2019 Watch out for those predators, because they are all around.\u201d </div> </div> </div>CofD has always been more about that second type of story. So it doesn't really matter if the protagonists know the things they're fighting, because the things they're fighting aren't the real monsters. The protagonists themselves are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T11:08:58-07:00","id":934606,"title":"","content":"If you want to retool your game towards a specific genre, there is a very good tool to do so: Conditions. Just by retooling your arsenal of Conditions, you can switch the mood of the game towards what you want without tweaking game mechanics. In general, your best tools to adjust things are Conditions and equipment bonus/penalties - game with harsh penalties will be harsher, games where you can get awesome bonuses for awesome will be awesomer, and so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T07:21:13-07:00","id":936073,"title":"","content":"I enjoy playing with different genres, so here are a few of my recommendations.<br /> <br /> <b>Integrity: </b>The Integrity system works with only a few genre-specific considerations. The main drama in many crime and noir stories involves the protagonists values, and the consequences of abiding by, or compromising those values. When determining the personal breaking points of the characters, establishing their sense of right and wrong is crucial. A hitman who refuses to do jobs against women and children, a Cop who plants evidence to convict a powerful mob boss, a small time con muscled into wearing a wire into a dangerous deal, all are the sort of ethical dilemmas that facilitate the sort of in-genre drama the Integrity system is set up to reward.<br /> <br /> <b>The Occult Skill:</b> As noted by other posters, there is nothing wrong with keeping the Occult skill as-is. However, many of the uses of Occult can be shifted to Academics if you decide to replace Occult with a different skill.<br /> Possible replacement skills could be <b><i>Security</i></b> (focusing on committing or defending against property crime such as Arson, Burglary, Trespassing) or <i><b>Tactics </b></i>(Focusing on combat between groups rather than individuals- this would be used largely by police and military characters, although it could extend to certain criminal groups).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T07:06:26-07:00","id":937582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/933374-what-to-take-out-of-the-system-if-not-using-it-for-supernatural-horror?p=936073#post936073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I enjoy playing with different genres, so here are a few of my recommendations.<br /> <br /> <b>Integrity: </b>The Integrity system works with only a few genre-specific considerations. The main drama in many crime and noir stories involves the protagonists values, and the consequences of abiding by, or compromising those values. When determining the personal breaking points of the characters, establishing their sense of right and wrong is crucial. A hitman who refuses to do jobs against women and children, a Cop who plants evidence to convict a powerful mob boss, a small time con muscled into wearing a wire into a dangerous deal, all are the sort of ethical dilemmas that facilitate the sort of in-genre drama the Integrity system is set up to reward.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with the &quot;genre-specific considerations.&quot; Without supernatural stressors, breaking points will rely solely on traumatic events, as your examples illustrate. PCs will have to keep that in mind at character creation (the PCs will be new to the system, so that shouldn't be too much of an issue).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/933374-what-to-take-out-of-the-system-if-not-using-it-for-supernatural-horror?p=936073#post936073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>The Occult Skill:</b> As noted by other posters, there is nothing wrong with keeping the Occult skill as-is. However, many of the uses of Occult can be shifted to Academics if you decide to replace Occult with a different skill.<br /> Possible replacement skills could be <b><i>Security</i></b> (focusing on committing or defending against property crime such as Arson, Burglary, Trespassing) or <i><b>Tactics </b></i>(Focusing on combat between groups rather than individuals- this would be used largely by police and military characters, although it could extend to certain criminal groups).</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I think I've been sufficiently convinced to keep Occult in as a skill. It'll can certainly be used as an are of knowledge for religion, cults, folklore, superstition, conspiracy theories, even cultural traditions. I'm not sure it'll have a huge place in my game or not, but I think not having that area of skill is worse than changing it something else.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12124-lord-dynel","name":"Lord Dynel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12124_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}